IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc-definitions`
IMPORT `roc4-order-19-div-1`
IMPORT `roc4-order-19-div-2`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), Order 19, Division 2 (rules 13 to 23): TESTS.
-- Every expected value is written from the text beside the assertion, before the run, and is not copied from the encoding's output.
-- Time: a judgment dated 27 January 2026 gives, 14 days after the date, a last day of 10 February 2026 (made-up input standing for O 3 r 3's answer).

-- ===== Rule 13 =====
`o 19 test div 2 DC trial of an originating claim` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `District Court`, `A District Judge`, `o 19 r 3(a) a trial`, `Originating claim`, FALSE
`o 19 test div 2 MC absent-parties case` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `Magistrate's Court`, `A Magistrate`, `o 19 r 3(a) a case where judgment is given or the action is dismissed at trial because one or more parties are absent`, `Originating claim`, FALSE
`o 19 test div 2 DC trial of an originating application` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `District Court`, `A District Judge`, `o 19 r 3(a) a trial`, `Originating application`, FALSE
`o 19 test div 2 MC damages by a District Judge` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `Magistrate's Court`, `A Magistrate`, `o 19 r 3(b) after damages are assessed or accounts are taken`, `Originating claim`, TRUE
`o 19 test div 2 MC damages not by a District Judge` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `Magistrate's Court`, `A Magistrate`, `o 19 r 3(b) after damages are assessed or accounts are taken`, `Originating claim`, FALSE
`o 19 test div 2 MC committal` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `Magistrate's Court`, `A Magistrate`, `o 19 r 3(c) an application for a committal order for contempt of court`, `Originating application`, FALSE
`o 19 test div 2 DC prerogative order` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `District Court`, `A District Judge`, `o 19 r 3(d) an application for a prerogative order`, `Originating application`, FALSE
`o 19 test div 2 GD judgment` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `General Division`, `A Judge`, `o 19 r 3(a) a trial`, `Originating claim`, FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 13(1) this Division applies to an appeal against a judgment of the District Court or Magistrate's Court` `o 19 test div 2 DC trial of an originating claim` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 13(1) this Division applies to an appeal against a judgment of the District Court or Magistrate's Court` `o 19 test div 2 MC absent-parties case` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 13(1) this Division applies to an appeal against a judgment of the District Court or Magistrate's Court` `o 19 test div 2 MC damages by a District Judge` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 13(1) this Division applies to an appeal against a judgment of the District Court or Magistrate's Court` `o 19 test div 2 MC committal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not named in paragraph (1): a trial of an originating application; damages not by a District Judge; a prerogative order; a General Division judgment; an appeal not to the General Division.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 13(1) this Division applies to an appeal against a judgment of the District Court or Magistrate's Court` `o 19 test div 2 DC trial of an originating application` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 13(1) this Division applies to an appeal against a judgment of the District Court or Magistrate's Court` `o 19 test div 2 MC damages not by a District Judge` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 13(1) this Division applies to an appeal against a judgment of the District Court or Magistrate's Court` `o 19 test div 2 DC prerogative order` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 13(1) this Division applies to an appeal against a judgment of the District Court or Magistrate's Court` `o 19 test div 2 GD judgment` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 13(1) this Division applies to an appeal against a judgment of the District Court or Magistrate's Court` `o 19 test div 2 DC trial of an originating claim` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) "lower Court" means the District Court or Magistrate's Court against which judgment an appeal is brought or being brought.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 13(2) a court is the lower Court` `District Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 13(2) a court is the lower Court` `Magistrate's Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 13(2) a court is the lower Court` `District Court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 13(2) a court is the lower Court` `General Division` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ===== Rule 14 =====
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(1) the period for the notice of appeal`'s `period length` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(1) the period for the notice of appeal`'s `period unit` EQUALS Days
-- Form 35, served on all interested parties; filed and served on the last day (10 Feb): in time.  The day after (11 Feb): out of time.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(1) the notice of appeal is filed and served as required` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(1) the notice of appeal is filed and served as required` TRUE TRUE (Date 11 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(1) the notice of appeal is filed and served as required` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 11 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(1) the notice of appeal is filed and served as required` FALSE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(1) the notice of appeal is filed and served as required` TRUE FALSE (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Extended to 17 Feb: 15 Feb is in time.  Shortened to 5 Feb: 8 Feb is out of time.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(1) the notice of appeal is filed and served as required` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 2 2026) (Date 15 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (JUST (Date 17 2 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(1) the notice of appeal is filed and served as required` TRUE TRUE (Date 8 2 2026) (Date 8 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (JUST (Date 5 2 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(2) the General Division may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(2) the General Division may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(2) the lower Court may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(2) the lower Court may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 14(2) the lower Court may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ===== Rule 15 =====
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(1) the period for the application for permission to the lower Court`'s `period length` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(2) the period for the application for permission to the General Division`'s `period length` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(3) the period for the notice of appeal after permission is granted`'s `period length` EQUALS 14
-- (1): permission required; applied and served on the last day: in time; a day later: out of time; permission not required: "Where" not met.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(1) the application for permission to the lower Court is made and served as required` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(1) the application for permission to the lower Court is made and served as required` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 11 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(1) the application for permission to the lower Court is made and served as required` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(1) the application for permission to the lower Court is made and served as required` FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The application went to a court other than the lower Court ("from the lower Court" is not met), everything else in order.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(1) the application for permission to the lower Court is made and served as required` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): the lower Court did not grant permission.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(2) the application for permission to the General Division is made and served as required` TRUE TRUE (Date 20 2 2026) (Date 20 2 2026) (Date 20 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(2) the application for permission to the General Division is made and served as required` TRUE TRUE (Date 20 2 2026) (Date 21 2 2026) (Date 20 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(2) the application for permission to the General Division is made and served as required` TRUE FALSE (Date 20 2 2026) (Date 20 2 2026) (Date 20 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(2) the application for permission to the General Division is made and served as required` FALSE TRUE (Date 20 2 2026) (Date 20 2 2026) (Date 20 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3): permission granted.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(3) the notice of appeal after permission is filed and served as required` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 6 3 2026) (Date 6 3 2026) (Date 6 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(3) the notice of appeal after permission is filed and served as required` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 7 3 2026) (Date 6 3 2026) (Date 6 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(3) the notice of appeal after permission is filed and served as required` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 6 3 2026) (Date 6 3 2026) (Date 6 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(3) the notice of appeal after permission is filed and served as required` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 6 3 2026) (Date 6 3 2026) (Date 6 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(3) the notice of appeal after permission is filed and served as required` FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 6 3 2026) (Date 6 3 2026) (Date 6 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(4) the General Division may extend the time for filing and serving an application for permission to appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(4) the General Division may extend the time for filing and serving an application for permission to appeal` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(4) the lower Court may extend the time for filing and serving an application for permission to appeal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(4) the lower Court may extend the time for filing and serving an application for permission to appeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 15(4) the lower Court may extend the time for filing and serving an application for permission to appeal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ===== Rule 16 =====
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(1) the appellant has provided security for costs and filed the certificate as required` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(1) the appellant has provided security for costs and filed the certificate as required` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(1) the appellant has provided security for costs and filed the certificate as required` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(1) the appellant has provided security for costs and filed the certificate as required` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(2) the appellants need to provide only one set of security for the appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(2) the appellants need to provide only one set of security for the appeal` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(3) the appellant must provide security for each respondent or each set of respondents` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(3) the appellant must provide security for each respondent or each set of respondents` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Three respondents, two of them by the same firm: two sets.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(3) the number of sets of security the appellant must provide` 3 2 EQUALS JUST 2
-- Two respondents by the same firm: "more than one respondent" is met, and they make one set.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(3) the number of sets of security the appellant must provide` 2 1 EQUALS JUST 1
-- One respondent: paragraph (3) does not apply, and a number cannot carry "no"; the yes/no function above answers JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(3) the number of sets of security the appellant must provide` 1 1 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): the forms of security.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(4) the security is in a form the text allows` `o 19 r 16(4)(a) a solicitor's undertaking in Form 37` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(4) the security is in a form the text allows` `o 19 r 16(4)(a) a solicitor's undertaking in Form 37` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(4) the security is in a form the text allows` `o 19 r 16(4)(b) a deposit in the Registry or with the Accountant-General` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(4) the security is in a form the text allows` `o 19 r 16(4)(c) any other form` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(4) the security is in a form the text allows` `o 19 r 16(4)(c) any other form` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5): $3,000 for a Magistrate's Court action, $5,000 for a District Court action.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(5)(a) the amount of security for a Magistrate's Court action` EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(5)(b) the amount of security for a District Court action` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(5) the amount of security the appellant must provide` `Magistrate's Court` EQUALS JUST 3000
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(5) the amount of security the appellant must provide` `District Court` EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(5) the amount of security the appellant must provide` `General Division` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(5) the security is in the amount the text requires` `Magistrate's Court` 3000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(5) the security is in the amount the text requires` `Magistrate's Court` 5000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(5) the security is in the amount the text requires` `District Court` 5000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(5) the security is in the amount the text requires` `District Court` 4999 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(5) the security is in the amount the text requires` `General Division` 3000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(6) a party may apply to the appellate Court to vary or waive the amount of security` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(6) a party may apply to the appellate Court to vary or waive the amount of security` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(7) the appellate Court may order further security for costs to be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 16(7) the appellate Court may order further security for costs to be given` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

