-- ===== Rule 18 =====
`o 19 test div 2 complete appellant's Case` MEANS `o 19 r 18(1) the appellant's Case` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`o 19 test div 2 appellant's Case without costs submissions` MEANS `o 19 r 18(1) the appellant's Case` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`o 19 test div 2 appellant's Case unsigned` MEANS `o 19 r 18(1) the appellant's Case` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 18(1) the appellant's Case contains what it must contain` `o 19 test div 2 complete appellant's Case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 18(1) the appellant's Case contains what it must contain` `o 19 test div 2 appellant's Case without costs submissions` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 18(1) the appellant's Case contains what it must contain` `o 19 test div 2 appellant's Case unsigned` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Respondent's Case: (a)(b)(c), then (d) intends to submit / states so, then (e)(f)(g).
`o 19 test div 2 complete respondent's Case` MEANS `o 19 r 18(2) the respondent's Case` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`o 19 test div 2 respondent's Case that raises (d) and says so` MEANS `o 19 r 18(2) the respondent's Case` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`o 19 test div 2 respondent's Case that raises (d) and does not say so` MEANS `o 19 r 18(2) the respondent's Case` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`o 19 test div 2 respondent's Case without a summary` MEANS `o 19 r 18(2) the respondent's Case` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 18(2) the respondent's Case contains what it must contain` `o 19 test div 2 complete respondent's Case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 18(2) the respondent's Case contains what it must contain` `o 19 test div 2 respondent's Case that raises (d) and says so` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 18(2) the respondent's Case contains what it must contain` `o 19 test div 2 respondent's Case that raises (d) and does not say so` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 18(2) the respondent's Case contains what it must contain` `o 19 test div 2 respondent's Case without a summary` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 18(3) the respondent is barred from making the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 18(3) the respondent is barred from making the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 18(3) the respondent is barred from making the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 18(4) the appellant's Reply contains what it must contain` (`o 19 r 18(4) the appellant's Reply` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 18(4) the appellant's Reply contains what it must contain` (`o 19 r 18(4) the appellant's Reply` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 18(5) the Case or Reply contains everything the party intends to put forward` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 18(5) the Case or Reply contains everything the party intends to put forward` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ===== Rule 19 =====
-- (1): Case 35, Case 35, Reply 20 pages; the limit itself is within, one over is not.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 19(1) the page limit` `o 19 r 19(1)(a) the appellant's Case` EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `o 19 r 19(1) the page limit` `o 19 r 19(1)(b) the respondent's Case` EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `o 19 r 19(1) the page limit` `o 19 r 19(1)(c) the appellant's Reply` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `o 19 r 19(1) the document is within the page limit` `o 19 r 19(1)(a) the appellant's Case` 35 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 19(1) the document is within the page limit` `o 19 r 19(1)(a) the appellant's Case` 36 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 19(1) the document is within the page limit` `o 19 r 19(1)(b) the respondent's Case` 35 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 19(1) the document is within the page limit` `o 19 r 19(1)(b) the respondent's Case` 36 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 19(1) the document is within the page limit` `o 19 r 19(1)(c) the appellant's Reply` 20 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 19(1) the document is within the page limit` `o 19 r 19(1)(c) the appellant's Reply` 21 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "unless the General Division otherwise orders": the order's limit is outside the text.
